Subject: [PATCH 07412/11362] [outer-loop] REQ-ARC-WMTE-5760/5766: spec entries
 + GAP-ARC-INDUCTION-REFINEMENT-NULL

Documents the two overnight CEGIS refinement-loop experiments (ThinkingCap-27B
+ Qwen-9B on GPU0, gemma-4-31B on GPU1, run in parallel per operator directive
to "swap models and try both again at the same time") whose artifacts were
already committed by a conductor auto-commit but never got spec entries or a
verifier_gaps.md update, since the long-running detached scripts wrote their
artifacts and exited without doing that documentation step.

Result on both models, independently re-verified: zero games improved from
refinement (positive_game_frac=0.0, wins=0), degradation guard holds on both.
Neither cleanly satisfies the pre-registered HONEST-NEGATIVE branch -- real,
disclosed nuances (memorization drops without a correctness gain; Qwen-9B's
emission rate just under the healthy threshold) keep both at
gate_branch=partial_inconclusive rather than a forced clean label.

This closes the design doc's open architectural question with a real
measurement: model capacity helps single-shot induction (gemma-4-31B's 0.378
vs ThinkingCap-27B's 0.188, both verified), but refinement compute does not
compound it. Logged as GAP-ARC-INDUCTION-REFINEMENT-NULL with the two
concrete next options (bigger/different model class, or reconsider explicit
up-front induction vs a reactive-with-verifier-as-filter architecture) --
both operator-only given the GPU-day-scale cost.

